---
import InnerLayout from '../../layouts/InnerLayout.astro';
---

<InnerLayout
  title="Systems & Integrations | EVO"
  description="EVO systems and integrations connect monitoring, control, software and technical platforms into one clearer operating layer."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <div class="page-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">SYSTEMS &amp; INTEGRATIONS</p>
        <h1>Connect the parts. <span>See the system.</span></h1>
        <p>When separate devices, sites or software tools need to work together, EVO can shape the integration layer around clear monitoring, control and future expansion.</p>
        <div class="page-hero-actions"><a class="page-button page-button-primary" href="/contact">Discuss an Integration ↗</a><a class="page-button page-button-secondary" href="/solutions">Back to Solutions</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="page-orb"></div><img src="/solutions/solution-systems-integrations.png" alt="" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container page-section-inner">
      <div class="page-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">CONNECTED CONTROL</p><h2>Integration without <span>unnecessary complexity.</span></h2></div><p>The objective is not to connect everything for the sake of it. The objective is to create a useful operating layer that makes systems easier to understand and manage.</p></div>
      <div class="card-grid-4">
        <article class="content-card"><span>01</span><h3>Monitoring</h3><p>Bring important states, alerts and operational information into one clear view.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span>02</span><h3>Control Integration</h3><p>Connect compatible controllers, devices and software through practical interfaces.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span>03</span><h3>Multi-Site Systems</h3><p>Structure visibility and access across branches, buildings or technical locations.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span>04</span><h3>Future Platforms</h3><p>Build integration layers that can support new EVO software products and services over time.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="split-section">
    <div class="container split-inner">
      <div class="split-copy"><p class="eyebrow">PLATFORM THINKING</p><h2>One clear layer over <span>many systems.</span></h2><p>EVO’s long-term platform direction is to keep specialized systems separate where needed, while exposing the right controls, data and workflows through clean interfaces.</p><div class="feature-list"><article><span>01</span><strong>APIs &amp; Interfaces</strong><p>Use structured connections instead of fragile one-off links.</p></article><article><span>02</span><strong>Permissions</strong><p>Keep control access intentional and appropriate to the user.</p></article><article><span>03</span><strong>Visibility</strong><p>Surface the information that actually matters for operation.</p></article><article><span>04</span><strong>Scalability</strong><p>Leave room for additional sites, modules and future services.</p></article></div></div>
      <div class="split-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="page-orb"></div><img src="/solutions/solution-systems-integrations.png" alt="" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">CONNECT · MONITOR · CONTROL</p><h2>Turn separate systems into <span>one clearer operation.</span></h2></div><a class="page-button page-button-primary" href="/contact">Talk to EVO ↗</a></div></section>
</InnerLayout>
